        {
          "type": "recap",
          "say": "To recap. A follower whose randomized timeout fires first runs for leader, and a majority of votes elects it. An entry is committed once a majority stores it. Stale logs can't win elections, so commits survive leader changes. And in a partition, only the majority side can make progress.",
          "props": {
            "title": "Raft, <em>in four lines</em>",
